{"title":"Career Roadmap · Public Health Officer","role":"Public Health Officer","summary":"A Public Health Officer (PHO) works on improving the health of populations rather than treating individual patients. The role combines health programmes, disease prevention, community outreach, epidemiology, health education, surveillance, data analysis and programme management.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Public Health (BPH / B.Sc Public Health)"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"“Public Health Officer” is a broad job title. Eligibility varies by government department, state, employer and specific recruitment notification. A BPH/B.Sc Public Health can provide a strong foundation, but some government or specialist public-health posts may require an MPH, relevant experience, or another specified qualification."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Public Health Officer (PHO) works on improving the health of populations rather than treating individual patients. The role combines health programmes, disease prevention, community outreach, epidemiology, health education, surveillance, data analysis and programme management."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical work areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Communicable disease control"},{"text":"Maternal and child health"},{"text":"Immunization programmes"},{"text":"Non-communicable disease prevention"},{"text":"Nutrition"},{"text":"Environmental health"},{"text":"School health"},{"text":"Community health programmes"},{"text":"Health surveillance"},{"text":"Health education"},{"text":"Public-health data management"},{"text":"Health programme implementation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"h","text":"BPH / B.Sc Public Health"},{"type":"h","text":"Community Health Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Field Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health / Programme Trainee"},{"ty